quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  6,152,"And do not come near the orphan’s property, except in the best manner, till he reaches maturity; and observe fully the measure and the balance with justice. We do not task a soul beyond its capacity. And when you speak, be just, even if it be (against) a relative, and fulfil the covenant of Allah. That is what He has commanded you, so perhaps you may become mindful (of advice)."
  6,153,"And indeed, this is My path, perfectly straight—so follow it, and do not follow (other) ways, for they will separate you from His way. That is what He has commanded you, so perhaps you may become God-conscious."
  6,154,"Then We gave the Book to Musa (Moses), to complete (Our blessings) upon those who are virtuous, and as an exposition of all things, and as a guide and a mercy, so that they may believe in the meeting with their Lord."
  6,155,And this Book that We have revealed is a blessed one. So follow it and be God-conscious so that you may be shown (His) mercy.
  6,156,"Lest you (pagans) say: ‘The Book was revealed only to two communities before us (i.e. the Jews and the Christians), and we were indeed unaware of their teachings.’"
  6,157,"Or lest you say: ‘If the Book had been revealed to us, we would have been better guided than they.’ Now, manifest proof, guidance, and mercy have come to you from your Lord. So, who is more unjust than he who rejects Allah’s revelations and turns away from them? We shall soon recompense those who turn away from Our revelations with a terrible punishment because of what they used to evade."
